    "text": "Two particles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of equal mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> are moving with the same speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in figure. They collide completely inelastic&nbsp;and move as a single particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> that the path of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> makes with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis is given by-<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0098_b804ef06b09c.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 261px;\" />"
